id: pm-gh1551
title: "GH-1551: expose omission and budget receipts on precise SDK read results"
description: "Public list, context, search and get first-page types omit runtime omission_receipt and optional default-budget receipts. Preserve precise required fields, option-sensitive whole-result omissions and producer continuations while exposing the shared public receipt contracts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: context-management,"gh:1551",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T06:27:39.130Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T07:52:40.720Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T07:52:39.943Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T07:52:39.943Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Root and query entrypoint consumers can inspect omission_receipt on list/context/search/get without casts; Default-budget read_output and output_budget_truncation are optional and typed; Explicit budget/session/cursor omission and sparse producer page narrowing remain sound; Packed declarations compile with the runtime receipt shapes.
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Expose shared raw-query receipt metadata and required finalized first-page omission receipts across public SDK entrypoints, preserving sparse producer and whole-budget omission types."
expected_result: Typed list/context/search/get consumers inspect omissions and applicable optional accounting receipts without redeclaring the host contract or losing first-page precision.
actual_result: "Pre-fix TS2339 controls now compile; packed root/core/query/contracts/runtime declarations, actual Node/Bun consumers and linked tests pass. Source headba0460507 passes all26required checks and exact100/100/100/100 hosted coverage."
